# Files Prettier must not touch.
#
# The rule this file encodes: Prettier formats source we author. Everything
# below is either not ours, not source, or regenerated by a tool that has its
# own opinion about layout — and formatting any of those produces a diff that
# comes straight back on the next build, extract, or oracle run.

# --- Markdown -------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberate, and the one exclusion here that is a judgement rather than a fact.
#
# Prettier's Markdown printer pads every table cell out to the width of the
# widest cell in its column. The panel table in AGENTS.md has a 260-character
# cell, so formatting that file takes its longest line from 80 to 296 — in the
# doc every agent and contributor reads first, which is hand-wrapped at 80
# throughout. 131 of the repo's 208 Markdown files contain a table. The printer
# also rewrites `*italic*` as `_italic_`, and neither behaviour is configurable.
#
# The prose here is hand-shaped and the tables are meant to be read in source,
# so this trades one-rule-no-exceptions for keeping the docs legible. Wrap prose
# at 80 by hand, as the existing files do.
*.md

# --- Vendored upstream sources -------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md > Porting discipline: do not edit vendored upstream source. These
# are the parity references; a reformat would make every future upstream diff
# unreadable.
/third_party/

# --- Build outputs --------------------------------------------------------
# apps/web/src/generated/ is wasm-bindgen output rebuilt by every pre* hook and
# both CI jobs; src-tauri/gen/ is written by Tauri's build script (its
# capabilities.json ships minified on one line); the rest is compiler and
# bundler output.
apps/web/src/generated/
apps/tauri/src-tauri/gen/
apps/web/.wrangler/
dist/
pkg/
/target/
/artifacts/
coverage/

# --- Lockfiles ------------------------------------------------------------
package-lock.json

# --- Shipped assets -------------------------------------------------------
# public/ is bytes served to the browser, not source, and every tracked file in
# it is generated: `i18n:extract` writes locales/en/* through i18next-parser and
# `i18n:stamp` writes the hashes (apps/web/CLAUDE.md forbids hand-editing them),
# and start/penguin-figure.json comes from scripts/generate-start-figure.mjs
# minified — Prettier expands it from 93KB to 108KB, on an asset the welcome
# screen fetches for every visitor.
apps/web/public/

# --- Test fixtures and captured data --------------------------------------
# Fixtures are data, not source. The `.golden.json` files are written by
# `bench_exact_solve --golden` and the detector oracle binaries with serde's own
# layout, so a reformat is reverted the moment a golden is regenerated.
tests/fixtures/
tests/corpus/
crates/**/tests/fixtures/
**/__fixtures__/
*.golden.json

# The tuner and the parity harness are captured, hand-tuned scratch pages.
apps/web/start-figure-tuner.html
packages/origami-simulator/bench/gpuParityHarness/index.html
